[s0l0!-header][h1]The While Loop[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

Ok, we've got the theory, let's look at a real example:[code format="js" codeId="671"]var i=0;
[b]while [/b](i<=10) {
   document.write(i + "<br />");
   i++;
}[/code]
The loop in this code will continue to run as long as i is less than, or equal to, 10. And each time the loop runs, it will increase by 1.

This will output the values from 0 to 10.[img id="2756" width="100%"]
[note][b]Heads up![/b]
Be careful when writing conditions. If a condition is always true, the loop will run forever![/note]
